{{also|Bellow}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{lb|en|US|dialectal}} {{l|en|beller}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|belwen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bylgian}}, ultimately from the {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}, whence also {{m|ang|belg||leather bag}}, {{m|ang|bellan||to roar}}, {{m|ang|blāwan||to blow}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|bellen||to bark}}, {{cog|ru|бле́ять||baa, bleat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɛloʊ/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɛləʊ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛləʊ|s=2}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bellow.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{examples|examples={{audio|en|Elkbellow.ogg|The bellow of an [[elk]]}}}}

# The [[deep]] [[roar]] of a large animal, or any similar loud noise.
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage=There was a tap at a door, a bull's '''bellow''' from within, and I was face to face with the Professor.}}

